1sp7uYyZF5TdWU01zs94wLAQ0HUKrfOai/view\">Interview 27.captions.srt</a>"], ["B-roll named above", "<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hwrFtt_HP95fNV3QwNFCaYQ888lV-bVQ/view\">MVI_4334.MP4</a> · <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NjqZ40LKxNb8RIV1MCaSDRElqPhKiUt0/view\">MVI_4340.MP4</a> · <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ho71zH9Vdbe2cnyL2FTa7NVgn1jghbBl/view\">MVI_4364.MP4</a>"]], "tech": [["Source", "3840×2160 UHD, 23.976 fps, HEVC (H.265) in Canon MP4, about 100 Mbps. Audio AAC stereo 48 kHz."], ["Timeline", "1080×1920 at <b>23.976 fps</b>. Same rate as the source. No frame-rate conversion."], ["Crop", "A 9:16 crop of UHD is 1215 px wide. Punch-ins up to 120% stay sharp. Do not go past 125%."], ["Audio", "Both channels are the same mic (dual mono, measured −28 dB mean, −6 dB peak on MVI_4307 and MVI_4329). Use either channel. Room is a large hall: take a noise print first, then noise reduction and a level pass before V1."], ["Loudness", "−14 LUFS integrated, −1 dBTP peak. Music 18–20 dB under the voice."], ["Captions", "Burned in, S4S style, same as your delivered Bronx and MOA 4EveryKid cuts. Brand teal <span class=\"mono\">#62CCBF</span>. US English. Big enough to read on a phone. Max 2 lines. Keep the bottom 20% clear."], ["Names", "Spell it <b>Soles4Souls</b> and <b>4EveryKid</b> on screen. The machine transcript writes “Souls for Souls” and “Souls4Souls”; that is wrong. The partner is <b>Conexión Américas</b> (the transcript writes “Connexion Americas”)."], ["Export", "H.264 MP4, 1080×1920. One file, 9:16 only. Upload to Frame.io → Ready for Review."]], "checklist": ["Frame 1 is Alex's face with the hook text already on screen. No logo, no fade, no title card at 0:00.", "Hook text reads exactly: Happiest I've ever been.", "Name super at 00:05, not at 0:00. Built as text you can change (surname to confirm).", "Only Alex speaks.", "Soles4Souls and 4EveryKid are spelled exactly on screen.", "Audio is cleaned (noise print, noise reduction, level pass) before V1.", "End card is the NEW S4S typography card. No logo anywhere before it.", "One file, 9:16 only."], "decisions": [{"t": "No visual reference on this shoot", "b": "Production Planning 13011943414 reads Requested, owner Nick. Until then the editor matches the delivered Bronx and MOA 4EveryKid cuts."}, {"t": "Alex's surname and exact title", "b": "He says “VP of International for Business Development”; his sticker reads ALEX. Nick confirms the surname and the title wording with Soles4Souls before the video posts."}], "client_note": "<b>Why this matters:</b> Soles4Souls wants a human hook that leads to the mission. Alex's hook is a career choice; the mission is the payoff in the last quarter.", "ask_examples": ["What is the hook text?", "Which line opens the cut?", "What goes on the name super?", "Can I use other staff in this cut?"], "transcript": "Machine captions (Erin's pipeline). Times are mm:ss from the first frame of the file. Soles4Souls is written wrong in them.\n\nMVI_4311.MP4 - Alex (VP International)\n[00:00] My name is Alex and I'm the VP of International for Business Development so I mean I take care of Europe, Asia and the\n[00:09] UK.\n[00:27] Oh so we're here to provide shoes to kids that belongs to family that are under\n[00:35] privileged and so in a nutshell we're here to provide shoes and put a smile on\n[00:40] those faces. One thing to say to people who support Souls4Souls is that we are\n[00:56] very grateful for your help. We are working at Souls4Souls but we couldn't do\n[01:02] what we're doing without you so thank you so much for your constant support\n[01:06] it's highly appreciated. My favorite part of working at Souls4Souls is that I\n[01:17] really managed to put my business skills being aligned with my values. I get to\n[01:24] use all the experience that I had in my previous career and serving people in\n[01:29] need and for me this is like the happiest I've ever been in any job.", "frames": {"f_4311_2": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "f_4311_60": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "f_4334_5": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "f_4311_85": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}}